            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "NewMexicoMama"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A simple and tasty dish! I also used olive oil instead of vegetable oil and added a pkg. of frozen corn (as used in the traditional mexican recipes) and about 1/2 cup chopped green chile for zing. Also added 10 minutes to the cooking time and served it with baked chicken. A perfect low-cal but filling dish! Thanks for the recipe!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kimiko"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This turns out so much better than it sounds. Great side dish to Mexican fare or Tex-Mex! Make ahead tip: I made this and then turned the stove off and let it sit in the pot for about an hour. 10 minutes before ready to serve, I transferred veggies to a baking dish, topped with cheese, covered with foil and placed in oven for a few minutes . Also used Mexican-style stewed tomatoes - lovely!",
            "datePublished": "2012-03-26T14:01:46.613Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mike H"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Oh man, this is some seriously good stuff. Tasty, Healthy, Delishous and Easy. 3 large zucchini are plenty, but the flavor and eye appeal is really enhanced by adding a cup of frozen corn. I doubled the garlic, onion and the stewed tomatoes. Use a flavored canned stewed tomato choice (Italian, garlic, etc). Will definitely make again. Will try adding a poblano pepper seeded and diced next time. Try not to overcook the squash so it keeps a little crispness to it. Flavor improves overnight and is also delicious cold. Great for an easy, cold lunch to take to work, or heat for dinner and add smoked sausage or chorizo.",
            "datePublished": "2017-01-15T17:41:28.250Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Richelle Grover"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used this recipe as a guide. Instead of stewed tomatoes I used fresh tomatoes from our garden and chicken broth for the liquid. I added some frozen corn and diced green chilies during the onion cooking step. Next time I think I will brown the onions to give the dish a little more depth. Thank you for posting this recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2019-08-19T02:10:35.733Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "John Trib"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used a scallion instead of an onion so not that big of a change, but my wife &amp; I prefer the scallion taste. I sliced the zucchini lengthwise then again in 1/4\" strips lengthwise and served in long, oval, individual dishes. Very nice presentation and tastes great!",
            "datePublished": "2019-02-21T18:13:33.430Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Schooldaze"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I wasn't happy with this one at first, then I put it in the oven on broil so that the cheese could get brown on top and it was pretty good that way! I'll try it again but next time I'll add more spice, maybe some cumin, and green chilis, then it should be delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2012-06-16T22:56:55.957Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LashGal"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved, loved, loved this!! I didn't need the cheese -- I liked it as-is! I didn't use stewed tomatoes, but fresh tomatoes and added enough chicken broth to just cover the bottom of my 10-inch skillet (I will use just a little less next time, though). I also added frozen roasted corn (as corn was suggested by the top review). I also used olive oil instead of vegetable oil. This is now one of my favorite ways to eat zucchini! I will definitely make this again, I could eat it alone for dinner!",
            "datePublished": "2009-08-26T21:46:56.440Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BudsGurls"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Mmmm...one of my favorite vegie side dishes when serving Mexican food! I slice my zucchini about 1/2\" thick, use butter, 1 clove of garlic, sprinkle a little seasoned salt &amp; substitute 1 can of original Ro-Tel instead of plain stewed tomatoes. I'll add some whole kernal corn when I have it but tastes great either way. Super quick, super easy &amp; muey delicioso!",
            "datePublished": "2012-05-13T08:27:37.217Z"
          },
          {
