              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "janmauss"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Glad I read all of the comments before getting started. I went with the can of RoTel someone suggested. I also like more onion, and definitely used a garnish of chopped fresh cilantro. As far as peeling and seeding the zuccchini, I always pick small ones, less than 6\" long and 1 1/4\" in diameter, which are so tender they don't need any of that extra work. Yellow summer squash works in this recipe, too, and again I pick the baby sized ones.",
